{"key":"enterprise/T1185","id":"T1185","name":"Browser Session Hijacking","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["collection"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may take advantage of security vulnerabilities and inherent functionality in browser software to change content, modify user-behaviors, and intercept information as part of various browser session hijacking techniques. A specific example is when an adversary injects software into a browser that allows them to inherit cookies, HTTP sessions, and SSL client certificates of a user then use the browser as a way to pivot into an…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1185","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--544b0346-29ad-41e1-a808-501bb4193f47","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.633Z","source_object_version":"2.1","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0067","name":"Logon Session Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0067","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9ce98c86-8d30-4043-ba54-0784d478d0b5","page":"telemetry/DC0067/"},{"id":"DC0088","name":"Logon Session Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0088","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--39b9db72-8b48-4595-a18d-db5bbba3091b","page":"telemetry/DC0088/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"